# Put the whole monitor in internal RAM.
#
# `noflash` maps this component's .text to iram0_text and its .rodata to
# dram0_data, so nothing in libmain.a is fetched through the flash cache.
#
# This is a correctness fix as much as a speed one, and the correctness half is
# the part that matters. Core 1's trap handler -- hyp_trap_entry in
# hyp_vectors.S, hypervisor() and everything it reaches -- used to live in
# flash. Any flash operation on core 0 disables the cache, and IDF's answer to
# that is to IPC the other core into an IRAM spin for the duration
# (spi_flash_op_block_func). Core 1 does not run FreeRTOS and cannot be parked
# that way, so a trap taken during a flash write would have fetched its handler
# through a disabled cache. Nothing writes flash at runtime today, which is the
# only reason that never fired; it is a landmine, not a design.
#
# The speed half: the trap path is the hottest code on the machine -- 345,906
# traps in a 45-second session, 542 cycles each -- and every one of them was
# subject to flash cache misses. IRAM has no misses.
#
# The DTB placeholder patcher, the romfs mapper and app_main() get pulled into
# IRAM too, which is a few KB of waste for code that runs once. Not worth a
# per-function annotation scheme to avoid; there is 768 KB of L2MEM and the
# whole component is tens of KB.

[mapping:main]
archive: libmain.a
entries:
    * (noflash)
